# Notes on Reliable Extraction

Reliable extraction is less about a single perfect rule and more about layered conservative signals.

Good readers preserve the page's intent while dropping repeated interface text.

## Practical Advice

Use fixtures for pages that look simple, pages that look noisy, and pages that barely have article structure.

## Comments

Reader comment: snapshots help catch regressions.

Another comment: selectors are useful for focused reads.
